     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-large-herbivores), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Reintroducing or increasing the populations of large wild herbivores – such as bison, elephants, and moose – in natural and degraded ecosystems alters habitats, potentially leading to greater carbon removal from the atmosphere and increased carbon storage in vegetation and soils. However, evidence of its effectiveness is limited and mixed.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-large-herbivores', null, null, null),
    ('3933adb5-41e2-57fc-9f40-a2cf8f7ab0f4'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement',
     'Your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Present more than one view fairly, and don''t run experiments with seawater or minerals.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Ocean alkalinity enhancement (OAE) increases the ocean’s natural ability to remove CO₂ from the air by increasing the alkalinity of ocean water. This carbon removal practice could be globally effective at removing CO₂ at the gigaton level annually and is currently being tested in field studies.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-alkalinity-enhancement', null, null, null),
    ('9f0aea98-532e-5160-8e48-eb1f76dcea68'::uuid, 'drawdown-deploy-ocean-electrochemistry',
     'Your list of questions and answers with sources.',
     'Research only; don''t try electrical experiments with water.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-electrochemistry), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Deploy Ocean Electrochemistry uses electricity to separate seawater into acidic and basic solutions, which can be used to remove CO₂ in different ways. Acidic streams can be used to alter the chemistry of seawater, either by releasing dissolved CO₂ for capture and long-term storage or by weathering alkaline rocks and increasing seawater alkalinity.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/deploy-ocean-electrochemistry', null, null, null),
    ('747455c5-6ce7-5aa0-9363-e3dd41f8e954'::uuid, 'drawdown-restore-whale-populations',
     'Your story with sources listed.',
     'Use reliable sources, and if you go whale watching, follow official viewing rules and distances.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-whale-populations), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Whales play a critical role in the ocean carbon cycle, but commercial whaling in the 20th century drastically diminished their populations. Restoring the abundance of whales to pre-whaling levels has been proposed as a way to remove additional CO₂ from the atmosphere and store it in the ocean.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/restore-whale-populations', null, null, null),
    ('91846487-707c-509d-b421-488fcd896853'::uuid, 'drawdown-bury-biomass',
     'Your summary with links to your sources.',
     'Research online or ask the agency; don''t dig, bury or burn anything for this mission.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/bury-biomass), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Biomass burial involves storing plant biomass, such as logs, woody debris, agricultural and forestry residues, and engineered bio-blocks, under conditions that prevent GHG-releasing decay – underground, above ground, or at ground level. Applications range from simple wood vaults buried underground to blocks of dried, compressed plant biomass sealed in impermeable barriers.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
     'https://drawdown.org/explorer/bury-biomass', null, null, null),
    ('7f666cb5-019d-5542-9809-9f8e606e13ab'::uuid, 'drawdown-use-methane-oxidizing-coatings',
     'A link or photo of your explainer with sources listed.',
     'Research and explain only; don''t experiment with gases or coatings.',
     'Solution summary from Project Drawdown (https://drawdown.org/explorer/use-methane-oxidizing-coatings), used with permission. Adapted: the mission wording is original.',
     'Photocatalytic methane-oxidizing coatings applied to roofs and other surfaces exposed to air can convert methane molecules that contact the surface into CO₂.',
     'Solution summary © Project Drawdown, used with permission.',
